1
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:06,380
(弗里曼) 宇宙之中 星球在不断爆炸
(Freeman) All around the Universe,stars are exploding.

2
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:11,050
这是宇宙大灾难
They are cosmic catastrophes.

3
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:13,250
但对这些科学家来说
But to these scientists,

4
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:16,120
它们是深空中的灯塔
they are beacons in the depths of space.

5
00:00:16,120 --> 00:00:18,160
它们宣示了两种神秘和 不可见的力量之间
They illuminate an epic battle

6
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:21,890
史诗般的战争
between two mysterious and invisible forces.

7
00:00:21,890 --> 00:00:25,900
其中之一 保证了我们自身的存在
To one we owe our very existence.

8
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:29,070
而另一种 则试图毁灭我们
The other is trying to tear us apart.

9
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:32,170
现在，我们正在为
Now we're in a struggle of our own

10
00:00:32,170 --> 00:00:35,440
理解这些巨大的力量而努力
to understand these colossal forces,

11
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:38,710
学会了解超越黑暗的真相
to learn to see beyond the darkness.

12
00:00:43,850 --> 00:00:49,090
空间，时间，生命本身
Space,time,life itself.

13
00:00:50,490 --> 00:00:55,930
宇宙的秘密，尽在穿越虫洞
The secrets of the cosmos lie through the wormhole.

14
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:58,930
♪穿越虫洞，第1x08集
♪Through the Wormhole 1x08♪

15
00:00:58,930 --> 00:01:02,930
超越黑暗
Beyond the Darkness

16
00:01:03,140 --> 00:01:08,410
你，我，太阳，星球—
You,me,the sun,stars --

17
00:01:08,410 --> 00:01:11,910
我们所见的物体均有一个共性
everything we see has one thing in common.

18
00:01:11,910 --> 00:01:13,910
我们都是由原子构成
We're all made of atoms.

19
00:01:13,910 --> 00:01:17,920
原子几乎构成了宇宙中 所知的全部物质
Atoms make up almost all the matter in the known Universe,

20
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:22,450
但是...宇宙中还有另外一类
but...There is a whole lot more to the cosmos,

21
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:26,120
一类我们刚刚开始观察的物体
a side we're only just beginning to see.

22
00:01:26,130 --> 00:01:31,200
我们的身体，我们的家庭 我们的世界
Our bodies,our homes,our world,

23
00:01:31,200 --> 00:01:33,070
甚至是巨大的空间内部
even the vast void of space

24
00:01:33,070 --> 00:01:36,000
都充满了一种神秘的东西
is teeming with a mysterious substance...

25
00:01:37,470 --> 00:01:39,540
...一种形态如此奇怪的物质
...A form of matter so strange

26
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:43,980
起初，许多科学家 甚至都曾经怀疑它的存在
that many scientists once doubted its very existence.

27
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:49,080
但是在2009年，一个 非常灵敏的粒子探测器
But in 2009,an incredibly sensitive particle detector

28
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:52,220
第一次发现了它
caught the first glimpse of it.

29
00:01:52,220 --> 00:01:54,190
这是一次震惊世人的发现
It's an Earth-shaking discovery,

30
00:01:54,190 --> 00:01:56,890
而且这一发现迫使我们
and it's forcing us to radically reassess

31
00:01:56,890 --> 00:01:58,460
重新审视 自己在宇宙中的位置
our place in the Universe

32
00:01:58,460 --> 00:02:01,690
以及我们自己的命运
and even our eventual fate.

33
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:06,160
小时候，我躺在卧室里时
As a boy,I used to lie in my room at night,

34
00:02:06,170 --> 00:02:10,440
时常害怕黑暗中 隐藏着什么东西
gripped by fear that something was out there in the darkness.

35
00:02:10,440 --> 00:02:12,500
那是一个怪物？
Was that a demon...

36
00:02:12,510 --> 00:02:16,210
或者只是椅子上挂的衣服？
Or my clothes slung over the back of a chair?

37
00:02:16,210 --> 00:02:20,310
我会用手电照亮 壁橱最远的角落
I'd shine my flashlight at the furthest corner of the closet,

38
00:02:20,310 --> 00:02:24,350
试图抓住所谓的幽灵
hoping to catch the phantom presence I sensed lurking there.

39
00:02:25,920 --> 00:02:29,090
呃，我从来没有 在暗处看到任何东西
Well,I never did find anything in the shadows.

40
00:02:29,090 --> 00:02:31,890
但是，看不到东西 并不意味着
But just because you can't see something

41
00:02:31,890 --> 00:02:34,390
没有东西
doesn't mean there's nothing there.

42
00:02:39,670 --> 00:02:43,440
1960年代，一个名为Vera Rubin 的年轻天文学家
In the 1960s,a young astronomer called Vera Rubin

43
00:02:43,440 --> 00:02:47,840
打算对一个少人问津的领域 进行研究
decided to explore an area of space that was little-studied.

44
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:52,640
有2个孩子，一个大约2岁 另一个大约4岁
I had 2 children,one almost 2 and one almost 4,

45
00:02:52,650 --> 00:02:55,250
我真的不喜欢
and I didn't like the idea

46
00:02:55,250 --> 00:03:00,220
和其他天文学家在 热门研究项目上竞争
of competing with astronomers for real hot topics.

47
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:02,050
(弗里曼)Vera Rubin知道
(Freeman) Vera Rubin knew

48
00:03:02,050 --> 00:03:05,260
如果她研究某些性感的东西 例如黑洞
if she studied something sexy,like black holes,

49
00:03:05,260 --> 00:03:08,990
其他的天文学家会 致力于战胜她的
other astronomers would end up beating her to publication.

50
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:13,130
于是她要另辟蹊径
So instead she began surfing the galactic backwaters.

51
00:03:13,130 --> 00:03:15,600
(Rubin)我自己并不十分确定
(Rubin) I'm not sure I really know

52
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:17,540
我为什么要研究星系
why I was studying galaxies,

53
00:03:17,540 --> 00:03:19,970
也许只是因为 它们在我看来非常神秘
except they seemed very mysterious to me,

54
00:03:19,970 --> 00:03:21,670
并且我们对它们所知不多
and there was not a lot known,

55
00:03:21,670 --> 00:03:24,480
特别是关于它们的运动 几乎是片空白
especially about their motions -- almost nothing.

56
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:28,050
(弗里曼)Vera的研究开始于
(Freeman) Vera first trained her telescope

57
00:03:28,050 --> 00:03:32,650
距离最近的河外星系 仙女座星云
on the Milky Way's closest galactic neighbor,Andromeda.

58
00:03:32,650 --> 00:03:37,220
与大多数星系一样 它有一个星球密集的核心区
Like most galaxies,it had a dense central bulge of stars.

59
00:03:37,220 --> 00:03:39,390
她预计，数十亿的星球
She expected the billions of stars

60
00:03:39,390 --> 00:03:41,560
就像太阳系里的行星 环绕太阳运行一样
circling around this central bulge

61
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:44,600
环绕着核心区运动
to orbit just like the planets in our solar system,

62
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:47,000
符合牛顿的引力定律
obeying Isaac Newton's laws of gravity.

63
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,100
距离中心越远
The further away they are from the center,

64
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:51,700
星球运行的越慢
the slower they orbit.

65
00:03:58,310 --> 00:04:00,710
(Rubin)这是大约40年前
(Rubin) This is a model of the solar system

66
00:04:00,710 --> 00:04:03,080
我老爹给我制作的
that my father built for me

67
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:05,350
太阳系模型
about 40 years ago,when he retired,

68
00:04:05,350 --> 00:04:09,490
展示了牛顿的理论
that shows exactly what Newton knew from his theories.

69
00:04:09,490 --> 00:04:11,560
这里的四个—
The four that you're seeing here --

70
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:14,430
水星，金星 地球，火星
Mercury,Venus,Earth,and Mars --

71
00:04:14,430 --> 00:04:18,630
火星是公转最慢的 地球次之
Mars is going the slowest,the Earth the next slowest.

72
00:04:18,630 --> 00:04:23,270
水星是公转最快的
Mercury is the most rapidly moving.

73
00:04:23,270 --> 00:04:27,540
因为火星受到的引力是 与水星受到的引力比较起来
Because the force of gravity is considerably less for Mars

74
00:04:27,540 --> 00:04:29,340
相对要小
than it is for Mercury,

75
00:04:29,340 --> 00:04:33,180
公转也就相应的更慢
the orbit is correspondingly slower.

76
00:04:33,180 --> 00:04:36,820
(弗里曼) Vera在对星系的研究中
(Freeman) This is exactly the pattern Vera expected to see

77
00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:39,950
也希望能够发现这样的公转模式
when she studied stars as they orbited in their galaxies.

78
00:04:39,950 --> 00:04:44,920
距离中心越远 移动的越慢
The further from the center,the slower they should be moving.

79
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:47,460
但Vera的发现并非如此
But that's not what Vera found.

80
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:51,700
(Rubin)我们花了大概2年时间
(Rubin) It took us about two years

81
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:56,430
得到了仙女座星云中 90颗星球的运行速度
to get velocities of 90 stars in the Andromeda galaxy.

82
00:04:56,440 --> 00:04:59,870
结果相当令人震惊
And the results were rather startling.

83
00:04:59,870 --> 00:05:02,410
我们发现所有的星星
We found that all of the stars

84
00:05:02,410 --> 00:05:04,940
运行速度是一样的
were moving at the same velocity,

85
00:05:04,940 --> 00:05:09,780
同样的速度 每秒250千米
the same number,250 kilometers per second.

86
00:05:09,780 --> 00:05:12,080
(弗里曼)接下来的几年间
(Freeman) For the next few years,

87
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:13,890
Vera观察的各个星系
every galaxy Vera looked at

88
00:05:13,890 --> 00:05:17,560
都给了她同样的疯狂结论
gave her the same seemingly crazy results.

89
00:05:17,560 --> 00:05:21,930
各个星系中 距离边缘不同的星球
All the stars all the way to the edge of the galaxies

90
00:05:21,930 --> 00:05:24,300
以同样的速度运行
were moving at the same speed,

91
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:28,200
和太阳系的规律完全不同
completely different from the way the solar system works.

92
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:29,670
唯一的解释是
The only explanation

93
00:05:29,670 --> 00:05:33,070
距离中心更远的星球
was that the force of gravity did not get weaker

94
00:05:33,070 --> 00:05:36,610
它们受到的引力并未减弱
the further a star was from the center of a galaxy.

95
00:05:36,610 --> 00:05:39,080
但是，这种情况只能在 一种条件下发生
But that could only happen

96
00:05:39,080 --> 00:05:44,320
那就是星系中存在着 天文学家看不到的物质
if the galaxies had more mass than astronomers could see.

97
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:47,990
(Rubin) 合理的解释是
(Rubin) The explanation was that there must be

98
00:05:47,990 --> 00:05:52,290
必须有相当多数量的 没有被观察到的物质
very significant amounts of matter that are invisible.

99
00:05:52,290 --> 00:05:57,860
实际上，星系中大概 90%或者95%的物质
In fact,perhaps 90% or 95% of the material in the galaxy

100
00:05:57,860 --> 00:05:59,360
都是不可见的
is invisible.

101
00:06:02,540 --> 00:06:06,340
(弗里曼)这可是一种 真正具有革命性的见解
(Freeman) This was a truly revolutionary idea.

102
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:10,680
星系中也许充满了 不可见的成分
Galaxies might be filled with an unseeable substance,

103
00:06:10,680 --> 00:06:15,510
科学家只能为其取名为 "暗物质"
something scientists could only think to call "Dark Matter."

104
00:06:15,510 --> 00:06:19,720
但是，这样一个新颖的理论 需要铁一般的证据
But such a radical theory demanded ironclad evidence.

105
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:23,690
很快，几十个天文学家 检查了Vera的研究成果
Soon dozens of astronomers were checking Vera's observations,

106
00:06:23,690 --> 00:06:26,090
努力去反驳她
either struggling to disprove her

107
00:06:26,090 --> 00:06:27,790
或者努力发现
or scrambling to discover

108
00:06:27,790 --> 00:06:32,100
这些神秘的暗物质 究竟是什么，究竟在何处
what or where this mysterious Dark Matter might be.

109
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:35,530
(Rubin)我发现它确实 很令人惊异，很有趣
(Rubin) I did find it amazing,and amusing,

110
00:06:35,530 --> 00:06:39,100
我选择这个研究领域
that I had picked this field because I was interested

111
00:06:39,110 --> 00:06:42,370
是因为我喜欢做 没人关心的课题
in doing something that no one would care about,

112
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:48,010
然而突然，我成了许许多多 天文学家争论的对象
and suddenly I was involved with lots and lots of astronomers

113
00:06:48,010 --> 00:06:53,180
这项研究成了一项热门话题
who had ideas and observations,and it was a hot topic.

114
00:06:55,790 --> 00:06:58,690
(弗里曼)在大西洋彼岸，英格兰
(Freeman) Across the Atlantic in England,

115
00:06:58,690 --> 00:07:00,860
顶尖宇宙学家Carlos Frenk
leading cosmologist Carlos Frenk

116
00:07:00,860 --> 00:07:04,060
开始研究暗物质的理论
began to investigate the idea of Dark Matter,

117
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:07,800
但是不是用望远镜 而是用数学工具
using not telescopes but equations.

118
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:10,740
利用牛顿的引力定律
Take Newton's laws of gravity and feed them

119
00:07:10,740 --> 00:07:14,040
进行高精度的计算机模拟...
into a highly sophisticated computer simulation...

120
00:07:14,040 --> 00:07:15,510
然后？吃个饭先...
Then go for lunch.

121
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:21,710
这是宇宙学机器 一个非常巨大的超级计算机
This is the cosmology machine,a very large supercomputer

122
00:07:21,710 --> 00:07:25,420
唯一的使命就是 模拟宇宙
whose only purpose is to simulate the Universe.

123
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:29,490
它是由1300台 同时工作的电脑组成的
It's made up of 1,300 computers all working together.

124
00:07:29,490 --> 00:07:32,590
即使这样，仅仅计算一小部分 宇宙的情况
Even then,it takes months

125
00:07:32,590 --> 00:07:36,900
也需要几个月的时间
to complete a simulation of a small part of our Universe.

126
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:41,070
这是可怕的计算能力 几乎超越了想象
This is awesome computing power almost beyond imagination,

127
00:07:41,070 --> 00:07:45,400
但是如果你想要仿真宇宙 就需要这么长时间.
but that's what it takes if you want to emulate the Universe.

128
00:07:46,610 --> 00:07:49,170
(弗里曼) Carlos的模拟计算
(Freeman) Carlos started out his simulation

129
00:07:49,180 --> 00:07:52,480
其初始条件是根据科学家 假设的宇宙初期状态
with what scientists think the early Universe was made of --

130
00:07:52,480 --> 00:07:56,750
在空间中漂浮着的 巨大气体云
a giant cloud of gas floating in empty space.

131
00:07:58,150 --> 00:07:59,880
他安坐椅中，等待
Then he sat back and waited

132
00:07:59,890 --> 00:08:03,150
等着看他的宇宙机器是否 能够建立起一个星系
to see if his cosmology machine could build a galaxy

133
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:05,420
就像我们现在所见的星系
like the ones we see.

134
00:08:05,420 --> 00:08:08,760
如果你试图利用我们 所见的材料
What happens if you try to make a galaxy in a computer

135
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:11,460
构建一个星系 会发生什么事？
using simply the material that we can see?

136
00:08:11,460 --> 00:08:16,170
发生的情况是，你以失败告终
What happens is,you end up with a failed galaxy.

137
00:08:16,170 --> 00:08:18,500
恒星出现，演变
Stars form,they evolve,

138
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:21,010
最大的恒星们出现 超新星爆发
the biggest ones explode as supernovae,

139
00:08:21,010 --> 00:08:22,870
它们放射出如此多的能量
and they inject so much energy.

140
00:08:22,880 --> 00:08:25,140
但是，没有足够的引力
But there just isn't enough gravity

141
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:26,910
无法使这些气体凝聚
to keep these gases together,

142
00:08:26,910 --> 00:08:30,320
于是星系分崩离析 不可避免
so the galaxy essentially blows itself apart.

143
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:33,850
气体消散，只有少量残余
The gas dissipates,leaving very little behind.

144
00:08:33,850 --> 00:08:37,860
我们的宇宙 不是这样形成的
This is not how our Universe is made.

145
00:08:39,330 --> 00:08:43,730
(弗里曼)于是Carlos开始 在他的公式中加入暗物质
(Freeman) So Carlos started to add Dark Matter to his equations --

146
00:08:43,730 --> 00:08:45,830
开始是一点，然后更多
first a little,then more,

147
00:08:45,830 --> 00:08:50,370
最终增加到普通物质的5倍
and eventually five times as much of it as visible matter.

148
00:08:50,370 --> 00:08:53,870
几周之后
After several weeks,

149
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:56,880
宇宙机器中 出现了奇怪的现象
something strange came out of the cosmology machine --

150
00:08:56,880 --> 00:09:00,810
奇怪之处在于它很熟悉
strange because it was so familiar.

151
00:09:00,810 --> 00:09:04,420
这是星系形成过程的 计算机模拟
This is a computer simulation of the formation of the galaxy,

152
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:08,350
现在有暗物质的作用 还有气体，在这儿，用绿色标出
now with invisible Dark Matter and gas,shown here in green.

153
00:09:08,350 --> 00:09:11,220
这是宇宙大爆炸后 10亿年的情况
About a billion years after the Big Bang,

154
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:13,160
一丛丛的暗物质
clumps of Dark Matter formed.

155
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:16,260
气体附着在这些暗物质丛中 形成了恒星
Gas fell into these clumps,turning to stars.

156
00:09:16,260 --> 00:09:18,460
被暗物质的引力吸引—
But attracted by the force of Dark Matter --

157
00:09:18,460 --> 00:09:20,230
不可见的暗物质，引力—
invisible Dark Matter,gravity --

158
00:09:20,230 --> 00:09:22,400
这些暗物质丛合并起来
these clumps came together,

159
00:09:22,400 --> 00:09:25,540
熔合成更大的结构
fused to build ever larger structures,

160
00:09:25,540 --> 00:09:27,970
100亿年之后
so that 10 billion years later,

161
00:09:27,970 --> 00:09:32,040
一个好像我们银河系的 美丽螺旋形星系建立起来了
a beautiful spiral galaxy like our Milky Way was formed.

162
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:34,050
(弗里曼)Carlos展示了
(Freeman) Carlos has shown

163
00:09:34,050 --> 00:09:37,850
在充满暗物质的条件下 星系可以建立起来
that galaxies should form when filled with Dark Matter.

164
00:09:37,850 --> 00:09:39,850
