330
00:17:38,230 --> 00:17:39,530
[ 烧胎 ]
[ Tires screech ]

331
00:17:39,530 --> 00:17:41,060
[ Electric motor whirs ]

332
00:17:53,010 --> 00:17:55,810
普通物质的表现 正和你期望的一样—
The ordinary matter behaved just like you'd expect it to --

333
00:17:55,810 --> 00:17:56,940
它停止了
it stopped.

334
00:17:56,950 --> 00:17:58,810
暗物质却完全不同
Dark Matter is fundamentally different.

335
00:17:58,810 --> 00:18:01,220
暗物质根本没有互相影响
The Dark Matter doesn't interact in any way,

336
00:18:01,220 --> 00:18:03,650
于是暗物质直接从碰撞中 穿行而过
so it just passed straight through the collision.

337
00:18:03,650 --> 00:18:04,820
继续前行
It kept on going,

338
00:18:04,820 --> 00:18:07,290
我们就看到暗物质 比停下的普通物质
and we now see it further from the point of impact

339
00:18:07,290 --> 00:18:09,420
运动到距离碰撞点更远的地方
than the ordinary material,which stopped.

340
00:18:09,430 --> 00:18:11,830
子弹簇是我们所掌握的 证明这些物质存在的
The Bullet Cluster is the best proof that we have

341
00:18:11,830 --> 00:18:13,290
最有力证据
that all this missing material

342
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:15,260
天文学家们研究了几十年
that astronomers have seen for decades

343
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:17,830
明白暗物质具有和普通物质 非常不同的特性
has very different properties to the ordinary matter.

344
00:18:17,830 --> 00:18:19,300
暗物质是全新的东西
It's something completely new,

345
00:18:19,300 --> 00:18:21,300
现有科学对它所知不多
and science knows very little about it.

346
00:18:21,300 --> 00:18:24,240
它感觉起来不像普通物质 它甚至感觉不到自身
It doesn't feel ordinary matter. It doesn't even feel itself.

347
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:26,810
当两坨暗物质互相冲撞
And when the two lumps of dark matter smashed into each other,

348
00:18:26,810 --> 00:18:27,880
它们根本不会注意到对方
they didn't even notice.

349
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:29,440
它们只不过是直接互相穿过
They just passed straight through.

350
00:18:29,450 --> 00:18:33,210
(弗里曼) 半个宇宙之外的大灾难
(Freeman) Cosmic disasters halfway across the Universe

351
00:18:33,220 --> 00:18:36,280
证明了暗物质的存在
have proved that Dark Matter is out there

352
00:18:36,290 --> 00:18:39,320
而且它们不像我们所知的 任何东西—
and unlike anything we know --

353
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:43,790
不可见，无法确定 就像个鬼魂
invisible,intangible,almost like a ghost.

354
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:46,030
我们是否能够找出个办法
Could we ever devise a way

355
00:18:46,030 --> 00:18:48,960
得以窥视这种 难以捉摸的物质？
to see a piece of this elusive substance?

356
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:52,000
有些科学家认为这是可行的
Some scientists believe it may be possible,

357
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,700
但要找到它 他们并不是在天空中寻找
but to find it,they're not looking up in the heavens.

358
00:18:55,700 --> 00:19:00,810
他们深入地下 地球的暗黑内部
They're headed down into the deep,dark bowels of the Earth.

359
00:19:04,540 --> 00:19:08,110
我们生活在 物质和光的宇宙中—
We live in a Universe of matter and light --

360
00:19:08,110 --> 00:19:11,980
物质组成我们 光支撑了我们
matter that makes us and light that sustains us.

361
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:16,250
现在我们知道 这只是现实的一小部分
But now we know that's only a small fraction of reality.

362
00:19:16,250 --> 00:19:18,720
我们的宇宙中充满了
Our Universe is also teeming

363
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:23,160
一种神秘组分 我们称之为"暗物质"
with a mysterious substance we call "Dark Matter."

364
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:26,830
我们看不见... 我们摸不着...
We can't see it... We can't touch it...

365
00:19:26,830 --> 00:19:28,730
但它无处不在
But it's everywhere.

366
00:19:28,730 --> 00:19:31,100
每一秒，数十亿的暗物质粒子
Billions of dark-matter particles

367
00:19:31,100 --> 00:19:34,570
穿过我们的身体
pass through our bodies every second.

368
00:19:34,570 --> 00:19:37,040
现在，如果科学手段能够设法
Now,if science can somehow

369
00:19:37,040 --> 00:19:40,940
俘获一个这种粒子 并且研究它
trap one of these particles and study it,

370
00:19:40,950 --> 00:19:43,810
那么我们也许会最终了解
then we might finally understand

371
00:19:43,820 --> 00:19:47,220
组成宇宙的大部分物质是什么
what most of the Universe is made of...

372
00:19:47,220 --> 00:19:50,990
而且搞清楚 它对我们的意义
And what this really means for us.

373
00:19:50,990 --> 00:19:53,120
在过去的世纪中
In the past century,

374
00:19:53,120 --> 00:19:56,360
物理学家努力工作 发现所有的物质
physicists have worked out that all matter is built

375
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:59,900
都是由大概20种 亚原子基本粒子组成
from about 20 basic subatomic particles.

376
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:01,430
名称诸如
They go by names

377
00:20:01,430 --> 00:20:05,440
玻色子，电子 夸克，中微子
like bosons,electrons,quarks,and neutrinos.

378
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:10,170
但是他们还怀疑 有其它的奇异的粒子存在
But they also suspect other more exotic particles exist.

379
00:20:10,170 --> 00:20:12,440
(Massey)目前有大量的
(Massey) There are plenty of theories out there

380
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:13,940
关于暗物质原理的理论
for what Dark Matter might be.

381
00:20:13,950 --> 00:20:16,050
我们列出清单
We're gradually working through the list

382
00:20:16,050 --> 00:20:18,120
一项项的考察，排除
and trying to rule them out one by one.

383
00:20:18,120 --> 00:20:19,580
这就是科学的方法
That's the scientific method.

384
00:20:19,580 --> 00:20:21,820
关于暗物质最时髦的理论是
The favorite theory for what Dark Matter is

385
00:20:21,820 --> 00:20:24,190
是超对称态粒子— 那就是说
is a supersymmetric particle -- that is to say

386
00:20:24,190 --> 00:20:26,660
所有我们已知的普通粒子
that all the ordinary particles that we know about

387
00:20:26,660 --> 00:20:28,390
都有这种类型的镜像
have this sort of a mirror image,

388
00:20:28,390 --> 00:20:30,330
宇宙中存在这类粒子
that there's this extra set of particles

389
00:20:30,330 --> 00:20:31,730
藏身于黑暗之中
that is in the dark sector

390
00:20:31,730 --> 00:20:34,100
与普通物质毫无干涉
that don't interact in any way with the ordinary material

391
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:36,400
只是发生很微弱的引力作用
except through the force of gravity,which is very weak.

392
00:20:41,270 --> 00:20:43,840
(弗里曼)科学家们给这些
(Freeman) Scientists have another name

393
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:46,240
暗物质粒子另起了个名字—
for these dark-matter particles --

394
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:49,950
微交互作用质粒子
weakly interacting massive particles,

395
00:20:49,950 --> 00:20:52,420
缩写为"wimps" （该缩写字面意为"懦弱者")
"wimps" for short.

396
00:20:52,420 --> 00:20:55,890
懦弱者们几乎不与 普通物质发生作用
Wimps hardly ever interact with atoms of normal matter,

397
00:20:55,890 --> 00:20:58,860
所以，俘获和研究它们 是一项很难的工作
so capturing and studying them is really hard.

398
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:00,520
[ 砰! ]
[ Boing! ]

399
00:21:00,530 --> 00:21:01,990
[ 嗖! ]
[ Zip! ]

400
00:21:01,990 --> 00:21:05,830
由于这个世界到处是 普通物质粒子
And since the world is full of particles of regular matter,

401
00:21:05,830 --> 00:21:09,300
很容易误捕到普通粒子
it's all too easy to end up snagging them by mistake

402
00:21:09,300 --> 00:21:12,240
而让懦弱者们溜之大吉
and letting the wimps get away.

403
00:21:14,870 --> 00:21:19,040
Dan Bauer发现了寻找懦弱者的 完美场所
Dan Bauer has found the perfect place to hunt for wimps --

404
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:24,610
在明尼苏达一个半英里深的 废弃铁矿中
down an abandoned Minnesota iron mine half a mile underground.

405
00:21:29,390 --> 00:21:31,390
我们现在在地下前进
We're now heading down underground

406
00:21:31,390 --> 00:21:33,620
进入Soudan地下实验室
into the Soudan Underground Laboratory.

407
00:21:33,620 --> 00:21:35,730
大概需要3分钟的旅程
It'll be about a 3-minute trip down.

408
00:21:35,730 --> 00:21:40,400
1960年之前
This is the same way the miners used to go down before 1960

409
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:42,570
矿工们也是这样下井的
to do the iron mining.

410
00:21:42,570 --> 00:21:46,000
大概有2341英尺深
It's about 2,341 feet underground,

411
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,070
也就是大概半英里
or about half a mile.

412
00:21:48,070 --> 00:21:51,210
你恐怕不会想到 在这里研究物理学
It's not the first place you'd think of to do physics,

413
00:21:51,210 --> 00:21:54,310
但是，另一方面 我们来这儿是有原因的
but,on the other hand,we're down here for a reason.

414
00:21:54,310 --> 00:21:57,680
在这里能够避免 来自空间的粒子干扰—
We're down here to avoid the particles coming from space --

415
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:59,880
也就是那些宇宙射线粒子
the so-called cosmic-ray particles.

416
00:21:59,880 --> 00:22:01,380
[ 嗡嗡声 ]
[ Buzzer sounds ]

417
00:22:01,390 --> 00:22:03,450
我们到了27层
We've arrived at level 27.

418
00:22:04,620 --> 00:22:06,860
(弗里曼) 你也许认为 半英里厚的岩床
(Freeman) You'd think half a mile of bedrock

419
00:22:06,860 --> 00:22:09,360
也许会足够深 能够阻挡住背景噪声
would be enough of a shield from background noise

420
00:22:09,360 --> 00:22:11,960
寻找懦弱者的工作 就会是小事一桩了...
to make wimp-hunting a cinch...

421
00:22:11,960 --> 00:22:13,160
但是，非也
But it's not.

422
00:22:13,160 --> 00:22:15,430
懦弱者探测器
The wimp detectors are buried

423
00:22:15,430 --> 00:22:18,700
埋设在几英尺厚的
inside several more feet of solid metal

424
00:22:18,700 --> 00:22:20,970
金属和重塑料护盾
and heavy plastic shielding.

425
00:22:20,970 --> 00:22:23,270
穿过岩石的洞穴
Throughout the rock of the cavern,

426
00:22:23,270 --> 00:22:25,680
穿过我们周围的材料 甚至我们本身
the materials around us,even in us,

427
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:28,350
仍有少量的辐射粒子
there are small amounts of radioactivity.

428
00:22:28,350 --> 00:22:30,610
这些粒子 如果它们进入我们的检测器
Those particles,if they got to our detectors,

429
00:22:30,620 --> 00:22:31,880
那就是巨大的背景
would be a huge background

430
00:22:31,880 --> 00:22:34,620
这样我们就无法看到懦弱者了
such that we would never be able to see wimps.

431
00:22:34,620 --> 00:22:35,890
而且，这个护盾
And this shield

432
00:22:35,890 --> 00:22:39,190
也在阻挡这些粒子 使之无法到达探测器
prevents those particles from reaching the detectors

433
00:22:39,190 --> 00:22:43,590
因为我们要找的是懦弱者
because we're trying to find wimps,not background particles.

434
00:22:43,590 --> 00:22:46,860
(弗里曼)在护盾内部
(Freeman) Inside the shield

435
00:22:46,860 --> 00:22:50,130
是一堆18个冰球大小的
is a stack of 18 hockey-puck-sized crystals

436
00:22:50,130 --> 00:22:51,700
实心锗晶体管
of solid germanium.

437
00:22:51,700 --> 00:22:55,810
它们被设计用来检测 如果有懦弱者进入
They're designed to pick up the faintest of vibrations

438
00:22:55,810 --> 00:23:00,380
这些锗原子时 产生的最微弱变化
if and when a wimp bumps into one of the germanium atoms.

439
00:23:00,380 --> 00:23:02,880
为了达到此目的
To have a chance of doing that,

440
00:23:02,880 --> 00:23:07,450
它们必须非常纯净，非常冷
they have to be ultrapure and ultracold.

441
00:23:07,450 --> 00:23:09,920
这是我们锗晶体的模型
This is our model of a germanium crystal.

442
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:13,960
这些网球代表了 晶体里的锗原子
These tennis balls represent the germanium atoms in the crystal.

443
00:23:13,960 --> 00:23:15,290
在室温条件下
And at room temperature,

444
00:23:15,290 --> 00:23:18,160
这些原子彼此之间
what's happening is that all of these atoms are moving

445
00:23:18,160 --> 00:23:19,500
相对运动
relative to one another.

446
00:23:19,500 --> 00:23:21,400
这就是我们所知的热运动
This is what we know as heat.

447
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:24,330
如果你将一个懦弱者 放入晶体，会发生什么？
What would happen if you tossed a wimp into this crystal?

448
00:23:24,340 --> 00:23:26,940
你几乎不会注意到变化
You wouldn't even notice the difference,

449
00:23:26,940 --> 00:23:29,610
因为晶体本身变化就很剧烈
because the crystal is vibrating so much.

450
00:23:29,610 --> 00:23:35,110
然而，如果将晶体冷却到 很接近绝对零度的程度
However,if I cool this crystal down to very near absolute zero

451
00:23:35,110 --> 00:23:39,220
原子的热运动就几乎停止了
so that the motion of the atoms stops,

452
00:23:39,220 --> 00:23:42,220
那么，如果有懦弱者进来
then if I toss our wimp into the crystal,

453
00:23:42,220 --> 00:23:44,820
我就看到晶体的变化
I see the vibration of the crystal,

454
00:23:44,820 --> 00:23:47,590
这就是我们要找的信号
and that's the signal we're looking for.

455
00:23:48,530 --> 00:23:50,030
(弗里曼)寻找这些
(Freeman) Looking for particles

456
00:23:50,030 --> 00:23:53,160
几乎不与普通物质 发生作用的粒子
that hardly ever interact with normal matter

457
00:23:53,160 --> 00:23:55,170
没有耐心的人 可干不了这个活儿
is not a job for the impatient.

458
00:23:55,170 --> 00:23:58,370
每秒钟，都有几千万的 懦弱者穿过我们
There are millions of wimps passing through us every second.

459
00:23:58,370 --> 00:24:00,740
由于他们交互作用很微弱
And because they're weakly interacting,

460
00:24:00,740 --> 00:24:02,070
它们仅仅是—
they do exactly that --

461
00:24:02,070 --> 00:24:04,640
穿过我们，继续赶路
they pass right through us and just go on their way.

462
00:24:04,640 --> 00:24:07,510
它们穿过整个地球
They pass through the entire Earth and go on their way.

463
00:24:07,510 --> 00:24:09,580
我们希望 每年有那么一两个粒子
We maybe expect one or two of these

464
00:24:09,580 --> 00:24:11,780
进入我们的探测器 产生作用
to interact in our detectors per year.

465
00:24:11,780 --> 00:24:13,780
难以置信的低概率
So,incredibly low rate.

466
00:24:15,920 --> 00:24:18,820
(弗里曼)为了避免错误
(Freeman) To help prevent false positives,

467
00:24:18,820 --> 00:24:21,960
数据记录在一个上了封条的
the data is blindly collected in a sealed box

468
00:24:21,960 --> 00:24:24,490
盒子中的计算机硬盘上
on the hard drive of a computer.

469
00:24:24,500 --> 00:24:28,000
一年之中，研究组中的任何人都
No one on the team is allowed to search it for wimp signals

470
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:30,130
不能搜索计算机上的信号
for an entire year.

471
00:24:30,130 --> 00:24:33,670
他们就只能干瞪眼 祈求好运
And then they look and hope.

472
00:24:35,140 --> 00:24:39,040
(Bauer)2007年，我们最后一次 打开盒子，啥子都没有
(Bauer) In 2007,when we last opened the box and found nothing,

473
00:24:39,040 --> 00:24:41,510
当然会有一点失望
it was certainly a bit disappointing

474
00:24:41,510 --> 00:24:44,950
因为我们的实验已经 搞了一年了
because we had been running the experiment for a year.

475
00:24:44,950 --> 00:24:48,920
但是，为了建立这个实验 我们花了大概7年
But it had taken us almost seven years to build the experiment,

476
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:52,860
所以如果在这点上 发现什么东西，那就太棒了
and so it would have been nice to find something at that point.

477
00:24:52,860 --> 00:24:57,030
(弗里曼)但是，花了7年时光 和几千万美元
(Freeman) But after seven years and tens of millions of dollars,

478
00:24:57,030 --> 00:24:59,460
Dan和他的研究团队 懦弱者抓捕队
Dan and his team of wimp catchers

479
00:24:59,460 --> 00:25:01,260
不会放弃
were not about to give up.

480
00:25:01,270 --> 00:25:04,900
在2009年底
And in late 2009,

481
00:25:04,900 --> 00:25:09,940
他们打开盒子 取出另外一整年的数据
they opened the box on another entire year's worth of data.

482
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:13,640
(Bauer)你在这个区域看到的
(Bauer) What you see in this region

483
00:25:13,640 --> 00:25:16,010
应该是背景辐射
is where the background radiation would be.

484
00:25:16,010 --> 00:25:18,280
有一些我们不感兴趣的事件
These are events we're not interested in.

485
00:25:18,280 --> 00:25:19,920
我们知道那不是懦弱者
We know that they're not wimps.

486
00:25:19,920 --> 00:25:21,220
在这个区域
In this area,

487
00:25:21,220 --> 00:25:24,690
在红色边缘，绿线之上
bordered by the magenta and above this green line,

488
00:25:24,690 --> 00:25:26,690
是我们应该发现懦弱者的地方
is where we should see wimps.

489
00:25:26,690 --> 00:25:29,490
如果这些是懦弱者候选人
If any of these are wimp candidates,

490
00:25:29,490 --> 00:25:32,830
它们会在我们打开盒子时变红
then they will turn red when we open the box.

491
00:25:34,600 --> 00:25:36,570
所以，我们仅仅点击过去
So,let's just click through.

492
00:25:36,570 --> 00:25:39,900
探测器上这个区域 没有任何红点
This detector doesn't have any red dots in that area,

493
00:25:39,900 --> 00:25:41,870
所以没有懦弱者候选人
so there are no wimp candidates.

494
00:25:41,870 --> 00:25:43,870
这个和这个都是如此
Same with this one and this one.

495
00:25:43,870 --> 00:25:45,340
啊，瞧瞧这儿—
Ah,but look here --

496
00:25:45,340 --> 00:25:48,080
这里真的显示了一个
we do have one that appears right here

497
00:25:48,080 --> 00:25:52,820
就在我们希望 懦弱者显示的区域
in the region that we would expect a wimp to appear.

498
00:25:52,820 --> 00:25:56,050
这儿没有 这儿没有
Nothing here. Nothinghere.

499
00:25:56,050 --> 00:25:58,020
嗷！ 但是看看这里
Oh! But look right down here.

500
00:25:58,020 --> 00:26:00,820
在这个区域里，有一点
We have one that just made it into the region

501
00:26:00,830 --> 00:26:03,260
就在我们认为的懦弱者区域
that we think is the wimp region.

502
00:26:03,260 --> 00:26:08,230
(弗里曼)两个事件 一年每天24小时的监测
(Freeman) Two events,two possible wimp impacts

503
00:26:08,230 --> 00:26:11,470
两个可能的懦弱者碰撞结果
in one year of 24-hour-a-day detecting.

504
00:26:11,470 --> 00:26:12,940
[ 乒! 乒! ]
[ Blink! Blink! ]

505
00:26:12,940 --> 00:26:16,770
史上首次 我们可能抓到了
For the first time,we may have actually trapped

506
00:26:16,770 --> 00:26:19,740
神秘暗物质的尾巴
pieces of this elusive Dark Matter.

507
00:26:19,740 --> 00:26:21,210
[ 乒! 乒! ]
[ Blink! Blink! ]

508
00:26:21,210 --> 00:26:23,310
这可能是在 了解暗物质本质路上的
This could be a giant leap

509
00:26:23,310 --> 00:26:27,580
巨大飞跃
toward understanding what Dark Matter really is.

510
00:26:27,590 --> 00:26:28,950
[ 噗! ]
[ Poof! ]

511
00:26:28,950 --> 00:26:30,920
但是Dan并不是100%确定
But Dan's not 100% sure

512
00:26:30,920 --> 00:26:34,260
他看到的是不是懦弱者
that what he has are even wimps at all.

513
00:26:34,260 --> 00:26:36,860
搜寻还要继续
So the search must go on.

514
00:26:36,860 --> 00:26:39,500
(Bauer)很令人激动
(Bauer) It's exciting,

515
00:26:39,500 --> 00:26:42,500
但作为科学家 激动之余必须保持淡定
but you have to temper that excitement as a scientist

516
00:26:42,500 --> 00:26:45,040
要意识到你还没有证明它
and realize that you haven't proven it yet.

517
00:26:45,040 --> 00:26:48,810
如果我们下一步能 看到好几个懦弱者
If we see half a dozen wimps,say,in this next run,

518
00:26:48,810 --> 00:26:51,370
我们就能决定性的说
what we will be able to say is,definitively,

519
00:26:51,380 --> 00:26:55,350
有暗物质跑到了Soudan下面来
there is Dark Matter getting down to this level of Soudan,

520
00:26:55,350 --> 00:26:57,780
这意味着地球被暗物质包围
which means that Earth is surrounded by Dark Matter

521
00:26:57,780 --> 00:26:59,550
银河系中存在暗物质
and the Milky Way has Dark Matter.

522
00:26:59,550 --> 00:27:03,020
如果找到了一个懦弱者 会开辟物理学的新疆界
If a wimp is found,it opens up a whole new range of physics.

523
00:27:03,020 --> 00:27:04,350
如果真的存在
If there is this extra

524
00:27:04,360 --> 00:27:06,590
这种超对称态粒子
supersymmetric class of particles out of there,

525
00:27:06,590 --> 00:27:08,120
它们有自己的规律
they're doing their own interruptions,

526
00:27:08,130 --> 00:27:09,960
它们自行其是 就是这样
they're doing their own thing,and that really,

527
00:27:09,960 --> 00:27:11,630
因为它们是宇宙中的主角
since it's the main stuff in the Universe,

528
00:27:11,630 --> 00:27:13,200
这就是宇宙中的现实
that's what's going on in the Universe.

529
00:27:13,200 --> 00:27:14,730
我们只是少数派
We're just the little bit on the side.

530
00:27:19,970 --> 00:27:22,210
(弗里曼) 但是，正当 科学家们感到
(Freeman) But just as scientists begin to feel

531
00:27:22,210 --> 00:27:24,240
暗物质触手可及时
they're getting a handle on Dark Matter,

532
00:27:24,240 --> 00:27:26,840
他们发现一些很奇怪的事
they discover something very strange.

533
00:27:26,840 --> 00:27:28,710
暗物质可能是
Dark Matter may be the stuff

534
00:27:28,710 --> 00:27:31,110
我们星系形成的原因
that's allowed our galaxy to form,

535
00:27:31,120 --> 00:27:33,550
但这还不是故事的结尾
but it's not the end of the story.

536
00:27:33,550 --> 00:27:35,750
在21世纪开始时
At the dawn of the 21st century,

537
00:27:35,750 --> 00:27:39,760
一个太空探测器发现 黑暗中隐藏的其它东西
a space probe found something else hiding in the darkness.

538
00:27:39,760 --> 00:27:43,060
在暗物质努力将 我们聚成形的时候
While Dark Matter strives to hold us all together,

539
00:27:43,060 --> 00:27:48,770
这个理论也许在准备 将整个宇宙摧毁
this force might be preparing to destroy the entire Universe.

540
00:27:53,940 --> 00:27:57,850
我们现在知道 可见的宇宙
We now know that the visible Universe

541
00:27:57,850 --> 00:28:00,410
就像是浮在巨大的 暗物质海洋
is nothing more than a layer of foam

542
00:28:00,420 --> 00:28:04,350
上的一层泡沫
floating on a vast sea of Dark Matter.

543
00:28:04,350 --> 00:28:08,490
天文学家发现他们 漂泊在这个不熟悉的海洋上
Astronomers find themselves adrift on this unfamiliar ocean.

544
00:28:08,490 --> 00:28:11,760
Saul Perlmutter已经在 水中航行了20多年
Saul Perlmutter has been navigating these waters

545
00:28:11,760 --> 00:28:14,830
试图找出
for the past two decades,trying to determine

546
00:28:14,830 --> 00:28:20,200
暗物质对我们的最终命运 究竟意味着什么
what Dark Matter might mean for our eventual fate.

547
00:28:20,200 --> 00:28:23,270
作为一个学物理的年轻学生
As a young student in physics,I very much wanted to measure

548
00:28:23,270 --> 00:28:25,210
我非常想研究那些看上去 很基本的物体
something that seemed fundamental,

549
00:28:25,210 --> 00:28:27,070
那就是 我们宇宙的命运是什么？
which is,what's the fate of the Universe?

550
00:28:27,080 --> 00:28:28,410
宇宙会永远存在？
Will the Universe last forever,

551
00:28:28,410 --> 00:28:30,750
或者某一天 它会挂掉，坍塌？
or someday will it come to a halt and collapse?

552
00:28:30,750 --> 00:28:33,750
(弗里曼) Saul选择沿着
(Freeman) Saul chose to walk in the footsteps

553
00:28:33,750 --> 00:28:36,480
20世纪最伟大的天文学家的 足迹前进
of the 20th century's most illustrious astronomer,

554
00:28:36,490 --> 00:28:38,720
埃德温 哈勃
Edwin Hubble.

555
00:28:38,720 --> 00:28:42,790
在1920年代 哈勃开始一丝不苟的
Back in the 1920s,Hubble began a meticulous survey

556
00:28:42,790 --> 00:28:46,660
测量夜空中几十个星系
of dozens of galaxies in the night sky.

557
00:28:46,660 --> 00:28:49,500
他发现了一些奇怪的事
But he noticed something strange.

558
00:28:49,500 --> 00:28:53,000
几乎所有的星系都偏红
Almost all of the galaxies were tinged red.

559
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:57,170
就像远离我们的物体 所发出的声音
Just as sound coming from objects moving away from us

560
00:28:57,170 --> 00:28:58,770
会变得更慢...
gets lower...

561
00:28:58,770 --> 00:29:00,880
[ 号声 ]
[ Horn blares ]

562
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:02,740
...光会变得更红.
...Light gets redder.

563
00:29:02,740 --> 00:29:06,910
哈勃推断 宇宙中所有的星系
Hubble deduced that every galaxy in the Universe

564
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:10,080
实际上都在远离我们
is actually hurtling away from us.

565
00:29:10,090 --> 00:29:15,460
只有一个结论 宇宙在扩展
There was only one conclusion -- the Universe must be expanding.

566
00:29:15,460 --> 00:29:17,990
但他无法确定扩展的速度
But he couldn't tell how fast.

567
00:29:17,990 --> 00:29:19,290
为什么
Why?

568
00:29:19,290 --> 00:29:22,100
因为距离近但是发光少的星系
Because galaxies that are close and relatively dim

569
00:29:22,100 --> 00:29:25,430
看上去和那些距离远 但是很明亮的星系差不多
look very similar to those that are far away but very bright,

570
00:29:25,430 --> 00:29:28,100
所以他无法确定星系的距离
so he couldn't judge their distance.

571
00:29:31,540 --> 00:29:33,670
当然，让人头疼的是
Of course,the tricky thing is that you need to know

572
00:29:33,680 --> 00:29:35,180
如果你要确定星系距离多远
how bright the actual galaxies are

573
00:29:35,180 --> 00:29:37,080
你要先知道它们有多亮
if you're going to tell how far away they are.

574
00:29:37,080 --> 00:29:38,550
如果你是一个 航行在大海上的水手
If you're a sailor out at sea

575
00:29:38,550 --> 00:29:41,250
你望着雾中远方的灯塔
and you're looking at a distant lighthouse through the fog,

576
00:29:41,250 --> 00:29:43,750
你不知道 是灯塔很亮
you don't know whether it's a very bright lighthouse

577
00:29:43,750 --> 00:29:44,950
距离很远
and you're very far away

578
00:29:44,950 --> 00:29:46,920
还是灯塔不太亮
or whether it's a very faint lighthouse

579
00:29:46,920 --> 00:29:48,060
而距离很近
and you're very nearby.

580
00:29:48,060 --> 00:29:49,990
这是一个基本的问题
This is the fundamental problem,then,

581
00:29:49,990 --> 00:29:51,960
上个世纪，天文学家们
that astronomers have had to struggle with

582
00:29:51,960 --> 00:29:53,260
都在纠结这个问题
through the last centuries.

583
00:29:53,260 --> 00:29:57,060
(弗里曼) 但这个问题 有个解决方法
(Freeman) But there is a solution to this problem.

584
00:29:57,070 --> 00:30:00,430
天体物理学家们 上个世纪80年代就知道了
Astrophysicists have known since the 1980s

585
00:30:00,440 --> 00:30:03,700
一个特别类型的恒星爆炸
about a particular type of star explosion

586
00:30:03,710 --> 00:30:07,010
称为1A型超新星
called a type 1A Supernova.

587
00:30:07,010 --> 00:30:10,180
当一个比我们的太阳 稍大的恒星
When a star slightly bigger than our sun

588
00:30:10,180 --> 00:30:12,150
烧光了燃料
runs out of fuel to burn,

589
00:30:12,150 --> 00:30:15,520
它溃缩成为一个暗淡的 高密度的状态
it shrinks down into a dimmer,denser state

590
00:30:15,520 --> 00:30:17,490
也就是白矮星
known as a white dwarf.

591
00:30:17,490 --> 00:30:22,020
它处在生与死之间
There it hangs in a netherworld between life and death.

592
00:30:22,020 --> 00:30:25,260
但是白矮星还有 重获新生的潜力
But the dwarf still has the potential

593
00:30:25,260 --> 00:30:29,500
如果它能够找到新燃料的话
to spring back into life if it can find fresh fuel.

594
00:30:29,500 --> 00:30:32,900
当白矮星是双星系统 中的一员时
When a white dwarf is part of a two-star system,

595
00:30:32,900 --> 00:30:35,970
临近的恒星可以提供燃料
the neighboring star can provide that fuel.

596
00:30:35,970 --> 00:30:38,610
一旦白矮星的引力
Once the gravity of the white dwarf

597
00:30:38,610 --> 00:30:41,340
从它的同伴那里攫取到 足够的物质
has snagged enough mass from its companion,

598
00:30:41,340 --> 00:30:43,510
就没有回头路了
there's no turning back.

599
00:30:43,510 --> 00:30:45,580
它会爆炸
It explodes.

600
00:30:46,950 --> 00:30:50,890
温度升高的十亿度以上
Its temperature rises to more than a billion degrees,

601
00:30:50,890 --> 00:30:55,790
它大部分的气体 发射进入太空
and most of its gas is blown off into space.

602
00:30:55,790 --> 00:31:00,030
这些1A型超新星 是达成我们目标的完美参照
These type 1A Supernovae are just perfect for our purpose

603
00:31:00,030 --> 00:31:02,530
因为它总是具有同样的质量
because it's always the same amount of mass

604
00:31:02,530 --> 00:31:05,770
当它爆发时
just when it explodes,and so it makes the same brightness

605
00:31:05,770 --> 00:31:07,200
也发出同样的光亮峰值
when it reaches its peak.

606
00:31:07,200 --> 00:31:10,140
它会明亮几周，然后在几个月的 时间里渐渐淡出
It brightens in a few weeks,it fades away in a few months,

607
00:31:10,140 --> 00:31:11,410
如果你能发现它
and if you can catch it

608
00:31:11,410 --> 00:31:13,710
观察这个现象
and watch just that little bit of an event,

609
00:31:13,710 --> 00:31:16,740
即使光线到达我们的时候 爆发已经发生了几十亿年
even billions of years later,when the light arrives at us,

610
00:31:16,750 --> 00:31:19,110
你也会有一个标准星 一个标准蜡烛
you have a standard star,a standard candle,

611
00:31:19,110 --> 00:31:20,580
这样就能用来确定距离了
to recognize distances with.

612
00:31:22,080 --> 00:31:25,690
(弗里曼)同样质量产生的 同样规模的爆炸
(Freeman) Brilliant explosions borne from identical mass,

613
00:31:25,690 --> 00:31:28,860
发出同样程度的光线
all giving off exactly the same amount of light.

614
00:31:28,860 --> 00:31:32,830
到达我们的光线量 就代表了星球离我们有多远
How much reached us should tell us how far away each was.

615
00:31:32,830 --> 00:31:35,630
原理上 这个理论应该管用
In principle,the idea should have worked,

616
00:31:35,630 --> 00:31:38,200
但是实践中有个问题
but in practice,there was a problem.

617
00:31:38,200 --> 00:31:40,500
(Perlmutter)现在 这听上去很不错
(Perlmutter) Now,it sounds great,

618
00:31:40,500 --> 00:31:43,170
但实际操作起来 就不是那回事儿了
but they're a real pain in the neck to work with.

619
00:31:43,170 --> 00:31:45,470
每一千年 在所观察的星系中
You only find a couple of them per millennium

620
00:31:45,470 --> 00:31:47,410
你只能看到十几次这种现象
in any given galaxy that you look at,

621
00:31:47,410 --> 00:31:49,540
而且你永远不知道 什么时候会出现
and you never know when one's gonna go off,

622
00:31:49,540 --> 00:31:50,680
所以，调配望远镜
so it's not very easy

623
00:31:50,680 --> 00:31:52,910
观察这一现象可不是个 简单任务
to schedule the largest telescopes in the world,

624
00:31:52,910 --> 00:31:55,020
那需要提前几个月预定
which have to be booked months in advance.

625
00:31:55,020 --> 00:31:57,280
"我想预定3月3号的望远镜"
It doesn't make a very good proposal to say,

626
00:31:57,290 --> 00:31:59,390
这可不是个好建议
"I would like the night of march the 3rd

627
00:31:59,390 --> 00:32:01,490
"因为在今后500年中的某个时刻
"because sometime in the next 500 years,

628
00:32:01,490 --> 00:32:03,020
超新星会突然爆发"
a supernova's going to explode."

629
00:32:04,160 --> 00:32:08,030
(弗里曼) 于是Saul和他的团队 灵感闪现—
(Freeman) Then Saul and his team had a flash of inspiration --

630
00:32:08,030 --> 00:32:11,030
每隔几周就拍摄完全相同的
take identical wide-angle pictures of the sky

631
00:32:11,030 --> 00:32:14,200
天空广角图像 然后利用自动化的程序
several weeks apart and use an automated program

632
00:32:14,200 --> 00:32:18,440
搜索超新星的闪光
to search them for the flashes of supernovas.

633
00:32:18,440 --> 00:32:20,510
(Perlmutter)这个主意成真的前提是
(Perlmutter) The idea being that if we could develop

634
00:32:20,510 --> 00:32:23,640
我们能够开发出足够精妙的 计算机软件
a sophisticated enough computer software,

635
00:32:23,650 --> 00:32:27,150
它能够比较图像中搜集到的
it could compare those thousands and thousands of galaxies

636
00:32:27,150 --> 00:32:29,120
几百万个星系
that we have in those images that we collected

637
00:32:29,120 --> 00:32:30,820
找出那个几周前还没 突然出现亮光的
and find the ones that had a new speck of light

638
00:32:30,820 --> 00:32:32,250
那一个星系
that wasn't there three weeks earlier.

639
00:32:32,250 --> 00:32:35,720
这些亮光可能就是超新星
And those specks would be the supernova discoveries.

640
00:32:35,720 --> 00:32:38,660
(弗里曼)在5年多的时间里
(Freeman) In just over five years,

641
00:32:38,660 --> 00:32:42,130
Saul和他的团队在 38个不同的星系中
Saul and his team spot 38 different stars

642
00:32:42,130 --> 00:32:45,400
发现了38个星球变成了超新星
in 38 different galaxies go supernova.

643
00:32:45,400 --> 00:32:49,400
他们发现超新星的能力
Their ability to spot these exploding fireballs

644
00:32:49,400 --> 00:32:50,770
名扬江湖
becomes legendary,

645
00:32:50,770 --> 00:32:53,140
当他们最终收集到足够的数据
and when they finally have enough data

646
00:32:53,140 --> 00:32:55,710
能够研究宇宙中 发生的事情时
to measure what is happening to the Universe,

647
00:32:55,710 --> 00:32:58,180
他们做出了自伟大的哈勃以来
they produce the biggest shock in astronomy

648
00:32:58,180 --> 00:32:59,910
天文学里最令人震惊的结论
since the great Hubble himself.

649
00:32:59,920 --> 00:33:02,450
目前，我们所有的图片说明
The picture that we all had at the time was,

650
00:33:02,450 --> 00:33:03,880
宇宙在膨胀
the Universe is expanding,

651
00:33:03,890 --> 00:33:06,020
宇宙中所有的东西
that all of the stuff in the Universe

652
00:33:06,020 --> 00:33:09,290
产生引力，彼此影响
gravitationally attracts all the other stuff in the Universe,

653
00:33:09,290 --> 00:33:11,460
所以引力应该减缓膨胀
so it should be slowing the expansion.

654
00:33:11,460 --> 00:33:13,990
过去的问题是 "膨胀会持续多久？"
The question has always been,"how far will that go?

655
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:16,660
持续多久？ 膨胀会在某天停止吗？
How long will it last? Will it slow to a halt someday?"

656
00:33:16,670 --> 00:33:19,130
但是当我们把观测的数据 绘制成图形时
What we found when we put the points on the plot

657
00:33:19,130 --> 00:33:21,670
我们发现情况完全超出想象— 膨胀根本没有减慢
was none of the above -- it wasn't slowing at all.

658
00:33:21,670 --> 00:33:23,670
显然的 实际上宇宙是在
Apparently,the Universe is,in fact,

659
00:33:23,670 --> 00:33:25,140
加速膨胀
speeding up in its expansion.

660
00:33:26,880 --> 00:33:29,210
(弗里曼)Saul的团队发现了
(Freeman) Saul's team had discovered

661
00:33:29,210 --> 00:33:31,580
一个完全超出期望和 无法解释的
a totally unexpected and unexplained

662
00:33:31,580 --> 00:33:33,210
存在于星系之间的斥力
repulsion between galaxies

663
00:33:33,220 --> 00:33:36,050
这个逐步的把宇宙分开
that is gradually blowing the Universe apart.

664
00:33:37,650 --> 00:33:40,350
他们称之为...
They called it...

665
00:33:40,360 --> 00:33:41,920
暗能量
Dark Energy.

666
00:33:41,920 --> 00:33:44,390
人们开始认为
It was startling to think that the Universe

667
00:33:44,390 --> 00:33:47,660
宇宙显然不是如我们所想
is apparently not mostly the stuff that we're used to seeing

